Placeholder. This file must hold the ASCII-armored PUBLIC key of the
release maintainer's tag-signing key ( §6, credential row
"Git tag-signing key").

It is EMPTY OF KEY MATERIAL on purpose. The release workflow refuses to
run while tools/release/tag-signing-fingerprint.txt reads UNPINNED, so
until the key ceremony has happened no release can be cut. A gate that
defaults to "allow" when unconfigured is not a gate.

To populate, after the ceremony:

    gpg --armor --export <fingerprint> > tools/release/tag-signing-key.asc
    gpg --fingerprint --with-colons <fingerprint> \
      | awk -F: '/^fpr:/ {print $10; exit}' \
      > tools/release/tag-signing-fingerprint.txt

Both files are PUBLIC. The private half never leaves the release machine
and never goes near a CI runner.

This key is NOT K1 (the release-manifest signing key), and it is not the
`releases@xchain.io` key that already exists in the platform docs. It
signs git tags only. Under D6 (single maintainer) it is the only release
control independent of the maintainer's GitHub account: the environment
approval comes from the same account that pushes the tag.
